  "criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "Technological Implementation",
      "score": 9,
      "reasons": [
        "Substantial working payment orchestration: retained actual PayPal sandbox pause/resume, sponsor capture then donor refund with active subscription, paid invoice/verified deduplicated webhook, restart-preserved signed receipt, and two-leg checkout with independent readbacks. The rehearsal reuses actual call/gate/checker/receipt modules with isolated mocks rather than a separate visual fiction.",
        "Complete paired task evidence is stronger than label-only accuracy: all 24 public cases are retained, current composed pipeline completes 12/12 versus 7/12 using identical execution modules, and exact-consent/script/money checks are visible in the harness. New explorer is a bounded static projection with one fixed GET, textContent rendering, complete-data checks and retained fallback.",
        "Deduction: the model contribution remains narrow and mixed. Original donor classification gate still fails at 11/12 with one wrong mutation label; purchase drafting 11/24 trails rules 14/24; model routing adds seconds. The outcome run is synthetic, guarded, direct-function and mock-money evidence, so its successful task result does not establish broad language reliability."
      ],
      "evidence": [
        "docs/results/functional-acceptance-2026-11-05/donor.json",
        "docs/results/functional-acceptance-2026-11-05/invoice-webhook.json",
        "docs/results/functional-acceptance-2026-11-05/receipt.json",
        "docs/results/guarded-checkout-2026-11-05.json",
        "src/rehearsal.js",
        "docs/results/donor-outcome-2026-11-06/harness-source.txt",
        "docs/results/donor-outcome-2026-11-06/outcomes.jsonl",
        "web/demo-tasks.js",
        "test/demo-tasks.test.js",
        "docs/DONOR-ROUTING-2026-11-06.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Design",
      "score": 8.5,
      "reasons": [
        "Native images show a consistent restrained visual system, clear primary relief action, legible money/status hierarchy and explicit unresolved state. The completed phone result places sponsor amount, unresolved refund and active gift together.",
        "New native phone comparison is a meaningful usability improvement: entire composed proposal, separate scripted Yes, confirmation and task result fit within the inspected viewport; desktop displays both arms together. Native selection, polite status updates and progressively disclosed execution traces support inspection.",
        "Deduction: the inline desktop recording text remains very small, especially on the phone entry. Some actual conversational design is also generic: both composed clarification tasks answer Sorry, I did not catch that rather than explaining the stated choices, and the hardship offer is long. These reduce the polish of the donor-facing experience despite safe execution."
      ],
      "evidence": [
        ".acceptance/rehearsal-evidence/final-mobile-complete-native.png",
        ".acceptance/rehearsal-evidence/task-demo-phone-hosted-native.png",
        ".acceptance/rehearsal-evidence/task-explorer-phone-hosted-native.png",
        ".acceptance/rehearsal-evidence/task-explorer-desktop-hosted-native.png",
        "web/demo.css",
        "docs/results/donor-outcome-2026-11-06/outcomes.jsonl"
      ]
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Potential Impact",
      "score": 7.5,
      "reasons": [
        "The after-hours nonprofit donor-care problem is concrete, and sponsor-first relief implements a plausible way to reduce immediate hardship while preserving the recurring gift. Actual sandbox completion and anonymously inspectable failure cases give the proposed mechanism credibility.",
        "The packet cites recurring-giving and retention context with appropriate cohort/year limits; it does not conflate these statistics with the app effect. Fresh exact consent, authoritative readback and unresolved handling address meaningful trust concerns.",
        "Deduction: likely benefit is still a hypothesis. No sponsor partnership, demonstrated demand, donor/staff observations, retention/time-saving improvement or willingness to pay is established. Equal gross capture/refund incurs fees, so coverage economics also depend on sponsor funding. These limit confidence in magnitude and adoption, not hackathon eligibility or prototype completeness."
      ],
      "evidence": [
        ".acceptance/relief-review-explorer-packet-20261106.md: Impact and alternatives",
        "docs/results/functional-acceptance-2026-11-05/donor.json",
        ".acceptance/rehearsal-evidence/final-desktop-complete-native.png",
        "docs/DONOR-OUTCOMES-2026-11-06.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Innovation/Idea",
      "score": 8,
      "reasons": [
        "The distinctive idea is the integrated donor-care transaction: conversational supported-action completion, sponsor-funded hardship refund while the gift stays active, exact fresh approval, sentence-backed claims and an independently verifiable app-signed record. Visible unresolved handling is part of the concept rather than an omitted error state.",
        "The new all-task comparison gives concrete evidence that model-assisted interpretation can enable supported paraphrase/context tasks that this keyword baseline misses, while code owns financial authority.",
        "Deduction: donor self-service and receipts already exist in named alternatives, and the evidence establishes an inventive integration rather than a new model or general autonomous negotiation advantage. Deterministic guards contribute to the composed system; the purchase price guard, not demonstrated AI-specific savings, selected the better plan."
      ],
      "evidence": [
        ".acceptance/relief-review-explorer-packet-20261106.md: Impact and alternatives",
        "docs/DONOR-OUTCOMES-2026-11-06.md",
        "docs/results/donor-outcome-2026-11-06/protocol.md",
        "docs/results/guarded-checkout-2026-11-05.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Presentation",
      "score": 8.5,
      "reasons": [
        "The current main entry tells one donor-relief story with direct rehearsal and receipt actions. The primary 73-second film has real-frame poster, captions and explicit provenance; older procurement/films are inside a closed optional archive.",
        "The main-page recorded explorer materially improves the AI demonstration: all 12 requests and both 24 outcomes, exact approval turns, baseline failures, route/time/proposal/write disclosures and withheld-consent notices are accessible at native reading size. It explicitly distinguishes recorded model requests, mock payments and retained sandbox receipt evidence.",
        "Deduction: the primary film itself remains rules-routed simulation plus a retained receipt and its desktop text is tiny at inline size. The visitor must use the separate explorer to inspect readable model-backed behavior. I inspected stills, captions and provenance, so motion continuity, narration quality and audiovisual pacing are not independently rated as if fully watched."
      ],
